# The Museum's candidates: classic synth sounds rebuilt from their published settings
# (decisions D88, D103, D104). A sound moves from here into resources/presets/12-museum.csbank,
# and so into the plugin, when the user admits it in a side-by-side on the audition page.
# This folder is not built into the plugin.
#
# DX7 E.PIANO 1 was admitted on 13 November 2026 (decision D107), DX7 BASS 1 (D111) and Prophet-5 Sync II and
# Brass (D115) on 14 November.

[Minimoog Fat Bass]
room = Museum
# "Emerson's Fat Bass from Brain Salad Surgery", from Tom Rhea's Sound Charts for the Minimoog
# (Moog Music, 1974, page 15). The chart: three sawtooth oscillators at full level, one at 32'
# and two at 16', tuned to unison; filter cutoff -2, emphasis 5, amount of contour 3.5, both
# keyboard-control switches on; filter contour attack 0, decay 300 msec, sustain 0; loudness
# contour attack 0, decay 600 msec, sustain 5; decay switch on, no glide. Play it an octave or
# two under middle C: the key is the 8' pitch, as on the instrument. One voice; a note joined
# to the one before it does not start the filter's sweep again, a note struck anew does, and
# that sweep at every struck note is the sound.
# The chart also has the filter-modulation switch on with the wheel a little raised: oscillator
# 3 shakes the cutoff at its own pitch, a growl more than a wobble. That is the ladder's FM
# here, a tenth of an octave either way.
# From the chart and the service manual: the oscillators, and the cutoff (-2 on the dial is
# about 250 Hz at the lowest key and follows the keyboard: 752 Hz at middle C by the manual;
# fitted 900). What the documents do not pin down is fitted to a recording of a real Model D
# set to this chart, played with every note struck: how far the contour opens the filter (2.5
# octaves; the manuals say between 1.4 and 2.2), emphasis 5 (0.06: little, with three
# oscillators driving the filter), the contours' times (the legend is close to the time a
# contour takes to finish), sustain 5 (0.65 of full), and how far oscillator 3 shakes the
# filter (the chart only draws the wheel "a little up").
# Still short of the recording: above 3 kHz the real one has a faint sizzle, 50 to 60 dB under
# the note, that the shake does not account for; a Minimoog's oscillators leak a little past
# its filter.
g1 = VA shape=saw oct=-2 level=0.8
g2 = VA shape=saw oct=-1 fine=3 level=0.8
g3 = VA shape=saw oct=-1 fine=-2 level=0.8
p1 = Ladder cutoff=902 res=0.06 key=1 drive=0 bass=0 fm=0.1
env1 = attack=1 decay=624 sustain=0.65 release=624 decayCurve=-1 releaseCurve=-1 velocity=0
env2 = attack=1 decay=450 sustain=0 release=450 decayCurve=-1 releaseCurve=-1
voice = env2ToP1=0.255 velToP1=0 drift=1
play = mode=legato priority=low
master = 0

[Minimoog Trilogy Lead]
room = Museum
# "Emerson, Lake and Palmer's Trilogy", from the same Sound Charts page. The chart: oscillator 2
# at 2' and level 8 carries the tune; oscillators 1 and 3 at 16', three octaves under it, at
# level 2; all three on the square wave; filter cutoff -1, emphasis 6, amount of contour 3, both
# keyboard-control switches on; filter contour attack 0, decay 800 msec, sustain 0; loudness
# contour attack 0, decay 400 msec, sustain 10; glide at 5, decay switch on. One voice, the
# lowest key sounds; a struck note starts the filter's sweep again, a joined one does not.
# From the chart: ranges, levels, switches. Fitted to a recording of a real Model D set to this
# chart, in which the player strikes every note: the pulse width (that instrument's "square"
# is nearer a third than a half: its second harmonic is strong and its third nearly gone), the
# cutoff (2.7 kHz at middle C; the dial reading alone would give 1.4 kHz), emphasis 6 (0.6),
# the contour's reach (1.7 octaves) and time. No glide: the chart has it on at 5, but in the
# recording each new pitch is there within a hundredth of a second, and a glide of even 25 ms
# made the notes' starts sound smoothed to the user.
g1 = VA shape=pulse pw=0.3 oct=-1 level=0.15
g2 = VA shape=pulse pw=0.28 oct=2 level=0.8
g3 = VA shape=pulse pw=0.3 oct=-1 fine=3 level=0.15
p1 = Ladder cutoff=2748 res=0.625 key=1 drive=4.5 bass=0
env1 = attack=1 decay=1140 sustain=1 release=1140 decayCurve=-1 releaseCurve=-1 velocity=0
env2 = attack=1 decay=3042 sustain=0 release=3042 decayCurve=-1 releaseCurve=-1
voice = env2ToP1=0.17 velToP1=0 drift=1
play = mode=legato priority=low
master = 0
